# Who may merge what.
#
# This file is the whole verification mechanism. There are no signatures and no
# keys, because those defend against somebody who controls this repository —
# and if that has happened they are already serving whatever they like to every
# client, including the next release's pinned keys. Access control is the
# mechanism; cryptography on top of it would be decoration.
#
# plugins.json is deliberately absent from this list: an addition to it merges
# on green CI, so an author lists their own plugin without waiting for anybody.

/verified.json      @abyssmemes
/CODEOWNERS         @abyssmemes
/.github/           @abyssmemes
/README.md          @abyssmemes
